{#- A link that has expired stands in the app's shell (design.md §12, "The boards are the
    desk", 2026-10-09; board ErrorsDesk): the bar with the one place a stranger may go,
    and the page on the desk under it. The other doors keep the lockup alone. -#}
{%- set desk = expired and not closing and not landing %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1{% if desk %}, viewport-fit=cover{% endif %}">
<title>targum</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('tokens.css') }}{{ asset('shared.css') }}{% if desk %}{{ asset('chrome.css') }}{% endif %}{{ asset('signin.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{%- if not desk %}
{{ chrome_face() }}
{%- endif %}
<script>{{ asset('keep.js') }}</script>
</head>
<body class="signin"{% if desk %} data-shell="desk"{% endif %}>
{%- if desk %}
{% set here = 'door' %}
{% include '_nav.html.j2' %}
{%- endif %}
<main class="gate">
  {%- if not desk %}
  {#- The lockup alone. There is no navigation to offer someone who is not in yet, and
      a header with three dead links is worse than no header. -#}
  <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="targum">
    <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
      <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span>targum</span>
  </a>
  {%- endif %}

  {#- The door itself is a card on the desk (§13, 2026-09-14): the lockup and the foot
      stand on the ground around it, the way the places and the footer do on every page
      behind it. -#}
  <div class="door{% if expired or closing %} whole{% endif %}">
  {#- What went wrong last time, where something did: a Google sign-in that was
      cancelled, took too long, or was for an address that is not on the guest list. Said
      on the door itself rather than on a page of its own, because the way out of every
      one of them is the form underneath. -#}
  {#- A sign-in through Google that took too long or didn't finish is a panel with its
      one way on, Sign in again (design.md §12, 2026-10-09); anything else said here is a
      line with the clay mark, ink rather than clay. -#}
  {%- if said and again %}
  <div class="fault-panel trouble" role="status">
    <p class="fault-panel-said">{{ said }}</p>
    <div class="fault-panel-row"><a class="fault-go" href="{{ again }}">{{ t("signin.page.sign-in-again", "Sign in again") }}</a></div>
  </div>
  {%- elif said %}<p class="said trouble fault-marked" role="status">{{ said }}</p>{% endif %}
  {#- Why they are here, when an app sent them: Connect in Claude or ChatGPT asks for an
      account first, and a door that said nothing about it looked like a different
      errand (copy audit, 2026-09-28). -#}
  {#- On the door itself the sentence is the heading (design.md §12, "The connector's
      pages are the boards'", 2026-10-09; board ConnApprove); on the page a mailed link
      opens, it stands over "Sign in as". -#}
  {%- if connecting and landing %}<p class="said connecting" role="status">{{ connecting }}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if landing and lost %}
  {#- A Connect lost on the way through the mail: started in another browser, or too long
      ago. A whole page with the clay mark, the reason, and the one press that signs in,
      as board ConnApprove draws it. -#}
  <svg class="fault-icon lost" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6.25"/><path d="M8 4.75v3.75M8 10.9v.1"/></svg>
  <h1>{{ t("signin.page.connect-lost-title", "We couldn't finish connecting") }}</h1>
  <p class="said">{{ t("signin.page.connect-lost-why", "You started in another browser, or too long ago. Sign in, then connect again from Claude or ChatGPT.") }}</p>
  <form method="post" action="/account/enter">
    <input type="hidden" name="t" value="{{ token }}">
    <button class="btn filled go" type="submit">{{ t("signin.page.sign-in", "Sign in") }}</button>
  </form>

  {% elif landing %}
  {#- The link arrived. Nothing has been spent yet: a mail client that fetches this page
      to preview it has only read it, and the account is opened by the button below. -#}
  {#- A break allowed before the "@", so a long address wraps at its seam rather than
      mid-word ("…gmai / l.com", 2026-09-28). The zero-width space is only in the
      heading; nothing is sent from it. -#}
  <h1>{{ t("signin.page.sign-in-as", "Sign in as {address}", address=landing.replace("@", "\u200b@")) }}</h1>
  <p class="said">{{ t("signin.page.press-to-sign-in-on-this-browser", "Press to sign in on this browser.") }}</p>
  <form method="post" action="/account/enter">
    <input type="hidden" name="t" value="{{ token }}">
    <button class="btn filled wide go" type="submit">{{ t("signin.page.sign-in", "Sign in") }}</button>
  </form>
  <p class="aside">{{ t("signin.page.didn-t-ask-for-this-you-can", "Didn't ask for this? You can close the page.") }}</p>

  {% elif closing %}
  {#- A whole page (design.md §12, 2026-10-09): an account inside its grace period is
      told so at every door, and the one way to keep it is a mail. -#}
  <h1>{{ t("signin.page.account-closing", "This account is being closed") }}</h1>
  <p class="said">{{ t("signin.page.to-keep-it-email-us", "To keep it, email us at hello@targum.page.") }}</p>
  <a class="fault-go" href="mailto:hello@targum.page">{{ t("signin.page.email-us", "Email us") }}</a>

  {% elif expired %}
  {#- A whole page too: a heading, one sentence, and the form whose one button sends a
      new link. Send a link stays ink, as the door's call to action (§9). The board's
      line icon over it, an envelope. -#}
  <svg class="fault-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M1.75 3.75h12.5v8.5H1.75zM1.75 4.25 8 9l6.25-4.75"/></svg>
  <h1>{{ t("signin.page.that-link-has-been-used", "This link has expired") }}</h1>
  <p class="said">{{ t("signin.page.each-link-works-once-for-twenty-minutes", "Enter your email and we'll send a new one.") }}</p>
  <form method="post" action="/account/sign-in" id="ask"{% if asked %} data-asked="{{ asked }}"{% endif %}>
    <label for="email">{{ t("signin.page.email", "Email") }}</label>
    <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email"
           autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="{{ t("signin.page.you-example-com", "you@example.com") }}">
    <button class="btn filled wide go" type="submit">{{ t("signin.page.send-a-link", "Send a link") }}</button>
  </form>

  {% else %}
  <h1>{% if connecting %}{{ connecting }}{% else %}{{ t("signin.page.sign-in-to-targum", "Sign in to targum") }}{% endif %}</h1>
  {#- One door was the rule here, and the reason was good: "Nobody has to work out which
      of two buttons they are." Google is a second door and not a second answer to that
      question — it proves the same address faster, and the account it reaches is the same
      account, because `person` is keyed on the address and nothing else
      (targum-internal#304).

      Drawn only where this install can finish the exchange. No Google script, no widget:
      an anchor to accounts.google.com, which is a link the reader chooses to follow and
      the one thing §11 lets off the page. -#}
  {%- if google %}
  <a class="btn ghost outline wide go with-google" href="/account/google">{{ t("signin.page.continue-with-google", "Continue with Google") }}</a>
  <p class="or">{{ t("signin.page.or", "or") }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
  <p class="said">{{ t("signin.page.no-password-we-ll-email-you-a", "No password. We'll email you a link.") }}</p>
  <form method="post" action="/account/sign-in" id="ask"{% if asked %} data-asked="{{ asked }}"{% endif %}>
    <label for="email">{{ t("signin.page.email", "Email") }}</label>
    <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email"
           autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="{{ t("signin.page.you-example-com", "you@example.com") }}">
    <button class="btn filled wide go" type="submit">{{ t("signin.page.send-a-link", "Send a link") }}</button>
  </form>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="said sent" id="sent" role="status" hidden></p>
  </div>

  {#- The foot the rest of the site has. Not navigation — there is still nothing to
      navigate to from out here — but somebody handing an address over deserves to read
      what happens to it before they do, which is what the privacy link is for once the
      documents are open. Until then this is the same three links as everywhere else. -#}
</main>
{#- Outside the door's column, as on every other page with it (2026-09-28). Inside, the
    foot laid out its columns by the window's width in a 26rem column, and ran them into
    one another. -#}
{% if desk %}{% include '_foot.html.j2' %}{% else %}{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}{% endif %}
{% if strings %}<script>window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};</script>
{% endif %}<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('fault.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('signin.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
